+
+### Downstream validation observation (#1749, 2026-11-14)
+
+A fresh downstream checkout's full check exceeded its enforced 720-second
+command limit while one metamorphic sample process remained active for
+more than six minutes after the other jobs drained. The process was
+starting rustc children, not dead. This was not a controlled benchmark: app
+builds and focused checks also ran during that attempt. The downstream fix
+pools the existing sample's case partitions without reducing its coverage.
+A full rerun and a quiet before/after timing are separate evidence gates;
+never report the timed-out attempt as passing or simply increase its cap.
